    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds fine in theory, but \"adopting clean tech\" costs a fortune upfront. most of us work on razor thin margins. it feels like the way these things are being framed, it's almost like the regulations are a given and we just have to figure out how to deal with them. don't you think there's a huge downside to forcing this kind of transition on people who didn't ask for it and can barely afford their electricity bills as it is?",
